{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>And you shall set it upon four pa'amot.</b> Rashi's explanation, of blessed memory, is that פעמותיו is as in its Targum, זוויתיה — its corners — for the rings were placed in the upper corners near the cover. The more correct view is what Ramban, of blessed memory, explained: פעמותיו is from the language of steps/strides, in the manner of (Song of Songs 7:2) ״מה יפו פעמיך״ — for the rings were placed in the lower corners near the base of the ark, since it was a matter of honor to elevate the ark on high, so that it would be borne and lifted above the shoulders of the priests, alluding to its archetype, which is exalted and uplifted, high and lofty above."], :book :exodus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:04:11.052890268Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}